**RAG for Research and Document Analysis**

This RAG system is built using LangGraph. 
Is purpose is to accurately extract and summarize text-based information retrieved from a library of pdfs, epub, txt, md, jpeg/jpg, png format documents.
During development, the model used for retrieval of documents and generation of responses was qwen3.8; the model used for grading and evaluation was a lighter-weight ption qwen2.5; for embeddings the nomic-embedding-model was used.
The workflow begins at ingestion of documents which loads the documents based on their type. After documents are loaded, they are vetorized into a ChromaDB vector database.
After ingestion the user can query a single question. The user can also start a chat. 
There is a checkpointer database for keeping track of a specific chat's history (a chat is associated with a thread-id), this enables the model to contextualize future responses.
There is also an in-memory cache so that the model does not have to retrieve the same documents again for a new query if what was previously retrieved contains relevant information.
The RAG is enhanced with concurrent grading which lowers the latency of the pipeline.

**How To Use:**

_potentially might want to use sudo_
 
cd Rag-for-Research-Analysis-Agent

docker service start

docker compose build rag

docker compose run --rm rag python -m app.main ingest // To ingest everything in library 
or
sudo docker compose run --rm rag python -m app.main ingest --rebuild-index // To clear the vector database first then re-ingest all documents in the library
or
sudo docker compose run --rm rag python -m app.main ingest --file "/documents/determined - robert sapolsky.pdf" // To ingest one specific document from the library 

docker compose exec ollama ollama pull qwen3:8b
docker compose exec ollama ollama pull nomic-embed-text

